<body>

{# ───── Pre-compute deck-wide values ─────
   Sample disclosure data, total cost, and headline finding all derive
   from the same aggregator the report uses — no separate code path. #}
{% set _pool = audit.sampling_config.n %}
{% set _sampled = audit.corpus_stats.sampled_conversations %}
{% set _dropped = (_pool - _sampled) if _pool >= _sampled else 0 %}
{% set _turns = audit.corpus_stats.sampled_turns %}
{% set _date_start = audit.corpus_stats.date_range_start.date().isoformat() if audit.corpus_stats.date_range_start else "" %}
{% set _date_end = audit.corpus_stats.date_range_end.date().isoformat() if audit.corpus_stats.date_range_end else "" %}
{% set _total_findings = aggregate.total %}
{% set _behaviour_findings = aggregate.behaviour_total %}
{% set _modules_firing = aggregate.modules_with_findings %}
{% set _duration_min = ((audit.completed_at - audit.started_at).total_seconds() / 60.0) if audit.completed_at else 0.0 %}
{% set _module_counts = {} %}
{% for s in sections %}
  {% if _module_counts.update({s.module.value: s.count}) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set _cost_ns = namespace(total=0.0) %}
{% for m, u in audit.token_usage.by_module.items() %}
  {% set _cost_ns.total = _cost_ns.total + u.usd_cost %}
{% endfor %}
{% if audit.token_usage.orchestrator %}
  {% set _cost_ns.total = _cost_ns.total + audit.token_usage.orchestrator.usd_cost %}
{% endif %}
{% set _total_cost = _cost_ns.total %}
{% set _primary_source = (audit.sources | first).value if audit.sources else "claude-code" %}
{% set _primary_path = audit.source_paths.get(audit.sources | first, "~/.claude/projects") if audit.sources else "~/.claude/projects" %}

<div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"><div class="progress-bar" id="progressBar"></div></div>

<main class="deck" id="deck">

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 1 — Cover ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide cover" data-title="Cover">
  <div class="reveal">
    <p class="slide-masthead">
      <span>Lucid Epistemic Audit</span>
      <span class="mast-divider"></span>
      <span class="mast-volume">Hackathon Demo · {{ audit.id }}</span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h1 class="cover-title reveal">Lucid.</h1>
    <p class="cover-deck reveal">An open-source epistemic audit for your personal AI conversation history — turning sessions and exports into a forensic intelligence brief.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cover-byline reveal">
    <span>Hackathon · Anthropic Build with Claude · Apr 21–26, 2026</span>
    <span class="byline-italic">Daniel Bentes · with Claude Opus 4.7</span>
  </div>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>Open with the artifact, not the pitch.</strong> Pull up the rendered HTML report on a second screen — the report IS the demo. Mention the deck is rendered from the same Python generator, sharing the same design tokens.
    <strong>Time:</strong> 30 seconds.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 01 · Cover</span>
    <span class="pagenum">01<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 2 — Premise ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Premise">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 01 · The premise</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal">Your assistant agrees with you.</h2>
  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); line-height: 1; font-weight: 600; color: var(--severity-high); margin: 0;">58<span style="font-size: 0.5em; color: var(--slate);">%</span></p>
      <p style="font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin: 0.6rem 0 0; max-width: 38ch;">
        of LLM responses across GPT-4o, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, and Gemini 1.5 Pro exhibit <em>sycophancy</em> in a 58k-prompt audit. Sharma et&nbsp;al., 2023.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="drop-cap" style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.7vw, 1.4rem); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 42ch; margin: 0;">
        Sycophancy isn't a bug in one model — it's a structural property of how RLHF rewards agreeable outputs. Across the literature it surfaces under different names: echo chambers, belief drift, perspective drift, cave-ins.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>The 58% figure</strong> is from Sharma et al. 2023 (<code>arxiv:2310.13548</code>). Across GPT-4, Claude 1.3/2, PaLM-2 — even after RLHF, all assistants reliably agree with stated user opinions even when objectively wrong.
    <strong>Anchor:</strong> "If your assistant agrees with you 58% of the time when it shouldn't, that's not a tool — that's a yes-man."
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 02 · The premise</span>
    <span class="pagenum">02<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 3 — Lucid one-sentence ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Lucid">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 02 · Lucid</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal" style="max-width: 26ch;">
    Lucid reads <em>your</em> conversation history and tells you exactly when, how, and how often the assistant agreed with you when it shouldn't have.
  </h2>
  <p class="reveal" style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem); color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; max-width: 64ch; font-style: italic;">
    Single CLI. Single static HTML report. No telemetry. Your data never leaves your machine except to call the Anthropic and Voyage APIs that score the findings. Open-source, MIT-licensed.
  </p>
  <div class="sidenote reveal" style="margin-top: 2rem; max-width: 70ch;">
    <p class="sn-title">Differentiation in one line</p>
    <p style="margin: 0;">Not a benchmark on test prompts — an audit on <em>your</em> actual conversations, with every finding citing a published research framework.</p>
  </div>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>Read the headline aloud, slowly.</strong> Hit "exactly when, how, and how often."
    <strong>If asked "isn't this just running an LLM on LLMs?":</strong> Yes — but the value is the COMPOSITION of seven research frameworks, calibrated against published baselines, with structured findings stored in SQLite for audit trails.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 03 · Lucid in one sentence</span>
    <span class="pagenum">03<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 4 — Seven frameworks ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Frameworks">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 03 · The research</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal">Seven published frameworks, one composition.</h2>
  <ol class="module-list reveal" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));">
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">A</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Spiral-Bench</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">17 assistant-side behaviours, intensity 1–3. <code>eqbench.com/spiral-bench</code></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">B</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Sharma 2023</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Paired-exchange sycophancy: feedback flips + answer cave-ins. <code>arxiv:2310.13548</code></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">C</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">SycEval direction</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Caves classified as progressive (correct) or regressive (worse). <code>AAAI AIES 2025</code></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">D</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Jain 2025 <em style="color:var(--slate);">(opt-in)</em></p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Cross-turn framing drift toward the user's worldview, no explicit agreement.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">E</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">BeliefShift</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Cross-conversation belief drift with evidence-vs-pressure attribution.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">F</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Influence Tactics Protocol</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">9-category user-prompt analyser: emotional triggers, urgency, false dilemmas.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">G</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Time / model attribution</p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Deterministic — every finding pinned to model + month. No LLM.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="ml-letter">H</span>
      <div>
        <p class="ml-name">Memory consistency <em style="color:var(--slate);">(novel)</em></p>
        <p class="ml-cap">Voyage retrieval + Opus classification of memory claims vs. corpus.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>Don't read every framework.</strong> Land on three: Spiral-Bench (A) for breadth, Sharma (B) for foundation, Memory (H) as the novel contribution.
    <strong>D is opt-in</strong> via <code>--include-module-d</code> (expensive). <strong>G is deterministic</strong> — no LLM.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 04 · Seven frameworks</span>
    <span class="pagenum">04<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 5 — Architecture ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Architecture">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 04 · Architecture</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal">Managed Agents orchestrator drives eight audit modules.</h2>
  <div class="three-col reveal" style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1rem 1.1rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin: 0 0 0.4rem;">Ingest</p>
      <h3>Local corpus parser</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.5;">~/.claude/projects (JSONL) + Claude.ai export (conversations.json + memories.json). Pydantic v2.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--ink); color: #f0e8d6; border: 1px solid var(--ink); padding: 1rem 1.1rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin: 0 0 0.4rem; color: var(--accent-soft);">Orchestrator</p>
      <h3 style="color: #fff;">Sonnet 4.6 · Managed Agents</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.86rem; color: rgba(240, 232, 214, 0.85); line-height: 1.5;">Custom-tool loop; routes work to per-module Opus 4.7 / Sonnet 4.6 calls. 8 client-executed tools.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1rem 1.1rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin: 0 0 0.4rem;">Persistence</p>
      <h3>SQLite store + report</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.5;">Findings checkpointed continuously. Idempotent re-runs. Static HTML report — no scripts.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="reveal" style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; max-width: 80ch;">
    Findings carry <code>citation</code>, <code>detected_by</code>, <code>prompt_version</code>, <code>prompt_hash</code>, Beta-posterior confidence intervals, and a SHA-256 idempotency key. Re-running doesn't duplicate findings — <code>UNIQUE (audit_run_id, module, conversation_id, turn_ids_hash, behavior)</code> rejects them.
  </p>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>The unusual choice:</strong> Managed Agents (still beta, header <code>managed-agents-2026-04-01</code>). Sonnet 4.6 routes via 8 client-executed tools. Corpus stays local.
    <strong>Critical detail:</strong> Sonnet 4.6 doesn't always reliably do multi-step tool chaining — added direct-invocation backfill. SQLite checkpoints continuously, idempotency key prevents duplicates.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 05 · Architecture</span>
    <span class="pagenum">05<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 6 — Audit loop CLI ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Audit loop">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 05 · The audit loop</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal">What happens when you run <code style="font-size: 0.65em; background: var(--bg-card); padding: 0 0.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule);">lucid audit</code>.</h2>
  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
    <ol class="step-list reveal">
      <li><strong>Parse + sample</strong><small>Stratified, recency-weighted sample. Default 100, configurable, <code>--sample all</code> for full corpus. <code>min_turns=5</code> filter (configurable).</small></li>
      <li><strong>Pre-flight cost estimate</strong><small><code>messages.count_tokens</code> (free) + per-module output budgets. Hard $20 gate; user must authorise above that.</small></li>
      <li><strong>Spin up Managed Agents session</strong><small>Sonnet 4.6 orchestrator + 8 client-executed tools. Live event stream into the CLI.</small></li>
      <li><strong>Run modules — checkpoint each finding to SQLite</strong><small>Idempotent. Failure mid-run never loses prior work. <code>--resume run-&lt;id&gt;</code> picks up where it left off.</small></li>
      <li><strong>Render report</strong><small>One static HTML file — no scripts, no external resources, CSP locks down inline JS. This deck rendered from the same generator.</small></li>
    </ol>
    <pre class="cli reveal"><span class="comment"># Audit a {% if _primary_source == "claude-code" %}Claude Code session corpus{% else %}Claude.ai export{% endif %}</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> uv run lucid audit \
    <span class="flag">--source</span> {{ _primary_source }} \
    <span class="flag">--path</span> {{ _primary_path }} \
    <span class="flag">--sample</span> {{ _pool }}

<span class="out">{{ _pool }} discovered, {{ _sampled }} sampled
Modules: A B C E F H
Cost:    <em>${{ "%.2f"|format(_total_cost) }}</em></span>

<span class="comment"># Live findings stream</span>
<span class="out">module A · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('A', 0) }}</em>
module B · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('B', 0) }}</em>
module C · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('C', 0) }}</em>
module E · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('E', 0) }}</em>
module F · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('F', 0) }}</em>
module H · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('H', 0) }}</em>
module G · <em>stored={{ _module_counts.get('G', 0) }}</em>
<em>✓ {{ audit.id }}.html
  {{ _total_findings }} findings · {{ "%.0f"|format(_duration_min) }} min</em></span></pre>
  </div>
  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>This is the demo moment.</strong> If possible, run <code>lucid audit --source {{ _primary_source }} --path {{ _primary_path }} --dry-run</code> live to show the cost-estimate flow.
    <strong>Real numbers from this run:</strong> {{ _sampled }} conversations, {{ _turns }} turns, {{ _total_findings }} findings, {{ "%.0f"|format(_duration_min) }} minutes wall-clock, ${{ "%.2f"|format(_total_cost) }} actual spend.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 06 · The audit loop</span>
    <span class="pagenum">06<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 7 — Sample disclosure (correctness) ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Sample">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 06 · The corpus we audited</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal">Honesty about what we read — and what we didn't.</h2>

  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
    <div>
      <aside class="sample-disclosure reveal" style="margin: 0;">
        <p class="sd-line">
          <span class="sd-label">Sample</span>
          <strong>{{ _sampled }}</strong> of <strong>{{ _pool }}</strong>
          conversations audited
          {% if _dropped > 0 %}
