        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stat-num">{{ _turns }}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">turns read end to end</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stat-num">{{ _behaviour_findings }}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">behaviour findings</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stat-num">{{ _modules_firing }}<span style="color: var(--slate-soft); font-size: 0.55em;"> / {{ aggregate.modules_total }}</span></div>
          <div class="stat-label">modules firing</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 1rem 0 0; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 56ch;">
        Date range: {{ _date_start }} → {{ _date_end }}.
        Source{% if audit.sources | length != 1 %}s{% endif %}:
        {% for s in audit.sources %}<code>{{ s.value }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
        Stratified by project, recency-weighted, seed={{ audit.sampling_config.seed }} — reproducible.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;">Conversations audited</p>
      <ul class="honor-roll">
        {% for cell in aggregate.fingerprint[:24] %}
          <li>{{ cell.conversation_short }}<span class="hr-turns">· {{ cell.finding_count }} finding{% if cell.finding_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% if aggregate.fingerprint | length > 24 %}
        <p style="font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--slate); margin: 0.6rem 0 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em;">
          + {{ aggregate.fingerprint | length - 24 }} more — full list in the report.
        </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>This is the answer to "did you cherry-pick?"</strong> Show the corpus stats. Show the actual conversation titles. Stress that the {{ _dropped }} excluded conversations are short one-shot exchanges (fewer than 5 turns) — not enough to develop an epistemic pattern.
    <strong>If asked why min_turns=5:</strong> Sycophancy and belief drift are multi-turn phenomena. A two-turn "what time is it" → "8pm" exchange has nowhere to drift to.
    <strong>Reproducibility:</strong> seed=42, stratified by project, recency-weighted. Same input → same sample.
  </aside>
  <div class="slide-chrome">
    <span class="runner">№ 07 · The corpus</span>
    <span class="pagenum">07<span class="total"> / 12</span></span>
  </div>
</section>

{# ───────────────────────── Slide 8 — The lede / signature finding ───────────────────────── #}
<section class="slide" data-title="Lede">
  <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="tick"></span>Volume 07 · The lede</p>
  <h2 class="display reveal" style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">What the audit actually found.</h2>

  {% if aggregate.headlines %}
  {% set lede = aggregate.headlines[0] %}
  <article class="lede reveal">
    <p class="lede-eyebrow">Lead finding · Module {{ lede.module_short }} · {{ lede.severity_class }} severity</p>
    <h3 class="lede-title">{{ lede.plain_english }}</h3>
    <div style="font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;">
      <span><span class="sev-dot sev-{{ lede.severity_class }}"></span>{{ lede.severity_class }}</span>
      <span>· <code>{{ lede.behavior }}</code></span>
      {% if lede.intensity is not none %}
        <span>· intensity {{ lede.intensity }} / 3</span>
      {% endif %}
      <span>· conf {{ "%.2f"|format(lede.confidence) }}</span>
      <span>· conv {{ lede.conversation_short }}</span>
    </div>
    {% if lede.quote %}
      <blockquote class="lede-quote">{{ lede.quote }}</blockquote>
    {% endif %}
    <p style="font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0.7rem 0 0; line-height: 1.55;">
      Cited via <em>{{ lede.citation_short }}</em>. Detected by {% for m in lede.evidence_blocks %}{% endfor %}Claude judge with self-consistency ensemble.
    </p>
  </article>
  {% endif %}

  <aside class="speaker-notes">
    <strong>Read the lede aloud.</strong> If a quote is shown, read the quote — it lands harder than the explanation.
    <strong>Severity logic:</strong> intensity 3 → high (oxide red), intensity 2 → mid (amber), intensity 1 → low (ink blue).
    <strong>Don't oversell:</strong> say "the assistant did this in this conversation" — not "the assistant always does this." Specificity is credibility.
  </aside>
